# Deviations from PROTOCOL_LEARN_SONNET.md

DL1 (after the run, before the report was read). 13 of 180 sessions did not attempt the task (Z 5, L 6, X 2). Each ran
only `cat task.md` and then replied that it had not run the task. The workflow subagents saw the orchestrator's
conversation context, and these 13 declined. None ran a tool script or submit.sh. They are invalid trials, not answers:
they are dropped from both calls and right. An issue's arm mean is taken over its remaining replicates. An issue with no
remaining replicate in an arm is dropped from that paired comparison. The replies are kept in
swe_sonnet/learn_replies.json.

DL2 (finding of the code-review audit, after the run). Every lesson in PROTOCOL_SWE_SONNET.md, here, and in
PROTOCOL_SWE.md (the Gemini run) was taught at the gold line number of that issue's own base commit. The workspace is
built from the 4a72da7 snapshot, so most lessons landed on unrelated code in the right file:
- 10 were not placed at all;
- only 29 of 114 landed on the code unit that holds the fix in the snapshot.
The L arm therefore tests a kit whose lessons were mostly misplaced. A corrected test is pre-registered separately as
PROTOCOL_LEARN_FIX.md.
